notes="The upright half treats opposite categories, the universal Ss-to-abelian functors, and a chain/cochain expression for F(X_*). The lower half is written a quarter-turn from the first and develops representability in two arguments and a phi/psi adjunction. The inclusion A subset A-hat and the inclusion of the functor category are visible single curved signs, not membership or equivalence. The repeated subscript on Delta-hat in this part is ab, not H’s ss. The lower embedding has a left hook but no visible right arrowhead; it is not silently made into a complete embedding arrow. Several Hom formulas are unfinished and remain so. The dual-looking C label, the third Hom subscript and the overwritten lower index on L are not mathematically repaired. The cancelled colimit trial reads delta both as index and final object. As a conditional mathematical check, if phi preserves the indicated colimits then Hom(phi(-),M) takes them to limits, since maps from a colimit are compatible families of maps; this explains the direction of the two limit arrows. It does not prove the representability assertion or existence of psi without additional hypotheses. The drawn phi/psi arrows agree with the displayed Hom(phi(X),M) isomorphic Hom(X,psi(M)). Staff ruling is part of the stationery, not underlining. Manuscript foot 356; no date or theorem heading."
